# The sdist carried `tests/` and could not run it. setuptools picked up the 118 modules at the top
# of `tests/` and nothing else: no `conftest.py`, so the evidence store was never redirected to a
# temporary directory and the torch-gated modules were never deselected; no `tests/fixtures/`, so
# every instrument that reads the GRPO record had nothing to read; no `tests/acceptance/`, which is
# where a package's stated condition is actually checked.
#
# Shipping the rest is not the fix either. Twenty test modules import the top-level `studies/`
# package through the `pythonpath = ["."]` setting in pyproject.toml, and `core/quantity.py` looks
# for the repository's `spec/` directory before it falls back to the copy inside the wheel. Making
# the sdist's suite runnable therefore means shipping `studies/`, `spec/`, `fixtures/` and `tools/`
# as well, which is the whole repository wearing a different name.
#
# So the sdist is the package, and the repository is where the suite runs. A half-suite that errors
# on collection is worse than no suite, because it reads as a broken library rather than as a
# deliberate boundary.
prune tests
